CNT4007 Project 1 - P2P File Sharing

Group Members:
Yash Narayan
Garrett Elebash

Build:
From the project root directory, run:

    make

This produces an executable named "peerProcess".


Setup:
Before running, make sure the following files are present in the
project root directory (same directory as main.cpp):

  - Common.cfg       (configuration file provided by the TA)
  - PeerInfo.cfg     (peer list provided by the TA)
  - <data file>      (the file to be distributed, name matches the
                      FileName field in Common.cfg)

Then run the setup script:

    bash setup_peers.sh

This reads PeerInfo.cfg, creates a subdirectory "peer_<id>" for each
peer listed, and copies the data file into the directory of every peer
whose "has file" flag is set to 1.


Running:
Start each peer in a separate terminal, in the order they appear in
PeerInfo.cfg:

    ./peerProcess 1001
    ./peerProcess 1002
    ./peerProcess 1003
    ./peerProcess 1004
    ./peerProcess 1005
    ./peerProcess 1006

Each peer prints status to stdout and writes its detailed event log to
log_peer_<id>.log in the project root. The peers terminate on their own
once every peer has received the complete file.


Notes:
- Tested on Linux (Ubuntu via WSL && Reptilian via VirtualBox). Built with g++ targeting C++20.